        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nevin McCaskill; Merv Krakau\n- Organizations: Buffalo Bills; New England Patriots; NFL\n- Places: New York; East Rutherford, New Jersey; Jefferson, Iowa; Capital District region of New York; United States\n- Roles: undrafted free agent; linebacker\n- Systems: MetLife Stadium; New York State Route 32B\n\nFacts:\n- Merv Krakau was born on May 16, 1951, in Jefferson, Iowa.\n- Merv Krakau is a former professional American football player who played linebacker for six seasons for the Buffalo Bills and the New England Patriots.\n- In 2007, Nevin McCaskill was signed by the Buffalo Bills as an undrafted free agent.\n- The Buffalo Bills are the only NFL team that plays its home games in the state of New York.\n- The New York Giants and New York Jets play at MetLife Stadium in East Rutherford, New Jersey, rather than in New York state.\n- New York State Route 32B was a state highway in the Capital District region of New York in the United States.",
